/-!
# A checked finite graph for the concrete binary icosahedral representation

The 120 rows pair matrices over `ZMod 121` and `ZMod 5`. Determinant checks
place every row in the product of the two special linear groups. Predecessor
paths prove that every row belongs to the subgroup generated by `(x,x5)` and
`(y,y5)`. Conversely, the four right-transition tables include multiplication
by each generator and its inverse, so closure induction proves exhaustiveness.
Two decoding functions certify that both coordinate projections are injective.
All finite checks use kernel reduction.

Source: the explicit candidate and paired enumeration saved in
`Scratch/qt1202_center_frattini/IcosahedralCandidate.json` in the parent
center–Frattini investigation. That enumeration supplies data only: all facts
needed for the graph certificate are verified here. This certifies the fixed
model of `CenterFrattiniSource.Model`, not a source theorem about SQTK groups.
-/

